# SFT execution status v0.98

2026-09-17. The approved new CPU-only Linux setup preflight completed on its
first attempt. It identifies insufficient free disk on the current disposable
runner. It is not a retry or a pass of native qualification.

Commit: `716774386cc3eba22f860c7699d6a33654882a02`.
Parent: `9ae708c73a327b7cac69c16d29d075450a500e9d`.
Exactly four new files were published; no existing files were modified/deleted.

## Observed result

[Preflight run 35211052193](https://github.com/saidi19/lumi-model/actions/runs/35211052193)
completed successfully, with `status=observed`, `code=disk_floor_insufficient`,
and `ready_for_unchanged_setup=false`. Workflow success means the diagnostic
completed, not that the disk or qualification was accepted.

- All source/helper/rootfs setup checks completed: 78 bound source files,
  successful process-local Linux subreaper setup.
- Both newly created empty temporary directories were identity-checked and
  removed. No ambiguous creation or cleanup failure was reported.
- Available disk: **14,347,816,960 bytes / 13.36 GiB**.
- Unchanged post-acquisition floor: **17,179,869,184 bytes / 16 GiB**.
- Required pre-acquisition free space, including allocation for the retained
  pinned TAR: **18,241,982,464 bytes / 16.99 GiB**. ZIP/TAR acquisition peak is
  also included in the calculation. Current shortfall: **3,894,165,504 bytes**.
- This is a measurement, not reserved capacity. Filesystem metadata and other
  writers can consume additional space.

This demonstrates the current runner's capacity blocker and is consistent with
the old coarse failure. It cannot retroactively prove the exact cause on the old
disposable host, whose disk measurement was not retained.

## Verification and CI

53 new synthetic tests and 40 unchanged harness/workflow regressions passed
locally on both Python 3.11.15 and 3.13.7. Ruff 0.15.1, workflow YAML parsing and
independent source review passed. The new workflow's own synthetic tests passed
on Linux before its single observation.

Only the named 651-byte artifact ZIP was downloaded, checked against GitHub's
digest, and decoded in memory. Its sole 1,004-byte closed JSON report was retained
with SHA-256 `448591aa8f0c33fef43e0b7540e929638bb1549ae725035d20341dc7c1de97c8`.
Two zero-network local verification passes accepted the observation, checked
seven plan bindings and confirmed ten previous source/evidence bindings unchanged.

[Source checks](https://github.com/saidi19/lumi-model/actions/runs/35211052158)
passed all four jobs, including the full selected Source suite.
[Spark checks](https://github.com/saidi19/lumi-model/actions/runs/35211052104)
also passed. All three workflows succeeded on their first attempt; none was
rerun. The remote branch tip was reverified after CI and matches the published
commit. No historical native workflow started for this commit.

## Next required fix

Use a CPU qualification host with sufficient free disk and headroom while
preserving the 16 GiB floor. Do not try another acquisition/full qualification
on the unchanged undersized runner. A fresh capacity-suitable host and a newly
authorized native attempt are required; this diagnostic does not authorize them.
GPU is not needed to resolve this disk/setup blocker.

Gate 5 remains incomplete. No software image was acquired by the probe, and no
Docker operation, child workload, GPU, real model/data read, or SFT training ran.
Source/Spark jobs and GitHub checkout/artifact transport are normal separate
network-using CI infrastructure; the zero-network claim applies to the probe.

